Z||000000||86SE||09-26-2000||09:11 PM||||I went to radio shack today and bought a pair of 4" x 10" speakers to replace the ugly 6x9's that were extruding out of the dash.  They are only 2 way (6x9 were 3 way) but they sound every bit as good thoe.<P>Cost me $14 a piece.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||4
Z||000001||Shiner||09-26-2000||11:08 PM||||Just be carefull about how much power you put through them.  The stock radio unit should be ok.  I replaced some drivers in two cheesy stereo speakers for my computer, and blew the crap out of them.  I don't think I was even putting ten watts into them either.<P> Good luck!||||reg||7
Z||000002||86SE||09-27-2000||09:10 AM||||Just as long as I don't hook em up to my amp!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I already fried 2 small 8" woofers (smoke was rolling from the box, melted the coil/cone) and my 700 watt sub is starting to go. :MAD:<P>But I just bought a 800 watt woofer.  So I should be fine for awhile.....||||reg||1
